\date{2024-07-26}
\taxon{Definition}
\author{fredrikbakke}
\title{detecting continuity}
\meta{source}{[[myers-riley-2023]]}
\import{common}

\p{
  A crisp type family #{G :_\flat I \to \Type} on a #{\flat}-modal and inhabited type #{I} is said to \concept{detect continuity} for #{\flat \dashv \sharp} if for every crisp map #{f :_\flat X \to Y}, #{f} is #{\sharp}-modal if and only if #{f} is [#{\flat}-orthogonal](fb-0045) to the counits #{{\varepsilon_{G_i} : \flat G_i \to G_i}} for every #{i :_\flat I}.
}
